For each `i` from 1 to `n`, we iterate from 1 to `i` and calculate the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `i - j * j`, where `j` is the square root of `i - j * j`. We then add 1 to the minimum number to get the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `i`.

Finally, we return `dp[n]`, which represents the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `n`.

